/T (Writable: streams to which data can be written \(for example, fs.createWriteStream\(\)\). Readable: streams from which data can be read \(for example, fs.createReadStream\(\)\). Duplex: streams that are both Readable and Writable \(for example, net.Socket\). Transform: Duplex streams that can modify or transform the data as it is written and read \(for example, zlib.createDeflate\(\)\).)
/E (Writable: streams to which data can be written \(for example, fs.createWriteStream\(\)\). Readable: streams from which data can be read \(for example, fs.createReadStream\(\)\). Duplex: streams that are both Readable and Writable \(for example, net.Socket\). Transform: Duplex streams that can modify or transform the data as it is written and read \(for example, zlib.createDeflate\(\)\).)
